### What this track proposes
This chore makes the jr-green role gate ignore one open review task, as Lending task 3.5 needs. Today the gate counts each task that is not `[x]` and has no `deferred` as incomplete. A helper, used only by the jr-green branch, ignores at most one `[~]` task whose text names `review-a`, `review-b`, `review-c`, `adversarial`, or `acceptance`. Every other gate, the SHA-evidence check, and the return shape of `phase_counts` stay unchanged. Red adds `tests/spec_review_gate/test_green_gate_review_task.py`, Green edits the checker, and the build session opens the pull request.

### How the current system works, per this spec
`phase_counts` in `skills/measure-orchestrator/scripts/measure_interphase_checks.py` reads one phase of `plan.md` and returns five counts: total, complete, in progress, incomplete, and complete with a SHA. A task is incomplete when it is not `[x]` and its text has no `deferred`. The jr-green branch fails with `current phase still has N non-deferred incomplete tasks` when the incomplete count is above zero. Mid-red, review-a, review-b, review-c, and phase-acceptance read the same counts, and final-acceptance uses `track_incomplete`. Lending rule A12 marks the review task `[~]` before Review A starts, so the open task 3.5 fails the jr-green gate.

### Findings
- F1 [Blocker] spec.md FR-1: FR-1 does not say if a name matches as a substring, as a whole word, or as the role label of the task. Define the rule. Add a Red case for near-miss text. Rationale: In Lending plans, `review a` matches 'review assignments' (lending-desk-bench measure/tracks/domain_trust/plan.md:83), and `acceptance` matches Red task 7.1 (measure/tracks/daily_model_schedule/plan.md:1126). A `[~]` Green task that says 'per the acceptance criteria' counts 1 today and 0 with a substring helper, so the gate passes in error. The bare words `adversarial` and `acceptance` already match each listed phrase form, so the intended rule is unclear.
- F2 [Major] plan.md Task 1.1 and spec.md FR-2: No Red case pins the `deferred` clause or the unchanged `complete > with_sha` check. The plan needs a case where a `[~]` Review A task holds `deferred`: the gate passes, as today. It needs the same case plus an unfinished `[~]` Green task: the gate fails. It needs a case with an `[x]` task without a SHA plus a `[~]` Review A task: the gate fails with the SHA message. Rationale: A helper that skips the `deferred` check makes `incomplete` equal to -1, and the branch treats -1 as true, so a passing plan fails. The same helper lets a deferred task use the one ignore, so an unfinished Green task passes.
- F3 [Major] plan.md Task 1.1: The old-result cases, the 'each named later role' case, and the Lending-shape case name no fixture or expected result. The mid-red case needs an open `[ ]` task and a `[~]` review task as the only `[~]` task; the result must not change. The review-a case needs all `[x]` tasks plus one `[~]` Review A task; the gate must still fail. State if 'each named later role' means the five names or all eleven forms. Write the Lending fixture into the plan from commit 6faaf42 of lending-desk-bench (`measure/tracks/domain_trust/plan.md`, lines 140 to 199). Rationale: A weak fixture passes even if `phase_counts` ignores the review task, and a Lending fixture needs each SHA on its marker line.
- F4 [Nit] spec.md FR-1 and FR-2: FR-1 says the gate ignores exactly one task, and FR-2 says at most one. With no qualifying task, the gate ignores none. Use 'at most one' in FR-1. Rationale: 'Exactly one' can mean 'ignore only when one task qualifies', and that reading gives a different count for two tasks.
- F5 [Nit] spec.md FR-3: The condition 'if other callers need it' has one answer. Mid-red (line 1293), jr-green (line 1334), and the review and phase-acceptance branch (line 1359) each unpack the five values of `phase_counts`. State that the five-value return stays. Name the code that the helper reuses: `phase_blocks` (line 371) and the task-line pattern that `phase_counts`, `track_incomplete`, and `discover_phases` repeat. Rationale: A condition hides a fixed fact, and a fourth copy of the pattern adds drift.
- F6 [Nit] spec.md FR-4 and Out of Scope: Three change-set points stay open. Out of Scope names 'the other tech-debt rows', but `measure/tech-debt.md` holds no row for this track and FR-4 lists none. FR-4 omits `CHANGELOG.md`, and earlier checker gate changes (commits f68a87f, 94698fe, 7e6dc79, and 27c2ed0) each added an entry. The fix reaches Lending only after the install of `~/.agents/skills/measure-orchestrator/scripts/measure_interphase_checks.py`, which Lending runs, and the spec is silent on that step. State each decision. Rationale: The earlier spec `audit_role_gate_allow_20261123` states its install step in FR-4.

